<!--
  ============================================================================
  AlienSpawnEnablers.xml                     Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-11
  ============================================================================

  WHY
  ===
  Debug "Spawn Pawn" lists PawnKindDefs, not xenotypes. Of the 74 Star Wars
  species that have a xenotype, only 43 are reachable through any pawnkind. The
  other 31 are fully-authored xenotypes nothing in the game can ever spawn, the
  Hutt among them. This file adds a dev-spawn pawnkind for the ones that are
  genuinely READY: they carry a head gene AND that head's art is present.

  READINESS METHOD, AND WHY IT IS NOT A FILE CHECK
  ================================================
  Testing "does the art exist" turned out to be the hard part. Vanilla art is
  packed into Unity bundles, so Core ships 2 loose PNGs and no Textures folder
  at all. Outer Rim Galactic Diversity keeps its 554 head PNGs under Common_Old,
  a folder its own LoadFolders.xml never lists, and they render anyway. A naive
  file-existence test gives false negatives in both directions; one built on it
  earlier would have neutralised dozens of working heads.

  So readiness here means the head art is EITHER directly on disk under a loaded
  Textures path, OR it sits in the same Outer Rim Heads folder as Bith and Mon
  Calamari, both confirmed rendering in game. Precedent, not inference.

  SHAPE
  =====
  Copied verbatim from Outer Rim's own OuterRim_MonCalamari pawnkind, proven to
  work on this stack. ParentName OuterRimTestColonyPawnKind verified present and
  Abstract=True (race Human, combatPower 40, defaultFactionType PlayerColony).

  Pointing at the BTD_ xenotypes deliberately: REMIX removes 100 duplicates with
  BTD preference and remaps 88 pawnkinds at runtime, so BTD_ is the side that
  survives. Naming it directly skips the remap.

  KNOWN COMPROMISES
  =================
  Several reuse another species' head, which is the upstream mod's choice, not
  ours: Lasat and Zygerrian use the Cathar head, Muun the Quarren head, Ortolan
  the Kubaz head, Nelvaanian the Bothan head. They spawn and look non-human, but
  not uniquely so.

  The two Sith entries are included only because they are technically ready.
  Given the campaign's Force rules they are the likeliest to be unwanted; delete
  those two defs if so.

  NOT INCLUDED, 18 species: Anzati, Echani and Falleen have no head gene at all;
  ChadraFan, Chiss, Defel, Feeorin, KelDor, Klatoonian, Nagai, Nautolan,
  Snivvian and the rest have a head gene whose art is absent. Those need art or
  a head reassignment first.

  ✏️ CORRECTION 2026-08-11 — GAMORREAN WAS MISCLASSIFIED ABOVE
  ============================================================
  The original list put Gamorrean under "head gene whose art is absent". Wrong on
  both halves, checked against the live GeneDef dump rather than the mod XML:

    - It has NO species head gene. Neither guy762_xenotype_gamorrean nor
      BTD_Gamorrean carries a guy762_Head_* gene at all.
    - Its head therefore comes from vanilla Jaw_Heavy, whose forcedHeadTypes are
      Male_HeavyJawNormal / Female_HeavyJawNormal — base-game art, always
      present.

  So the Gamorrean was renderable the whole time; it just renders as a heavy-jaw
  human with a flat pig-nose decal. It is now handled properly one directory
  over in GamorreanPawnKinds.xml, which gives it real armed pawnkinds rather
  than a dev-spawn stub, so no Jawa_Spawn_Gamorrean entry is added here.

  Worth re-testing the same assumption against the other 17: this misfire came
  from checking for a species head gene's art without first checking whether a
  species head gene exists.

  ⚠️ These inherit defaultFactionType PlayerColony from the parent. Correct for
  dev spawning, WRONG for world generation. Real Hutt Cartel presence needs
  faction work, tracked separately in faction_roster_v2.md.
  ============================================================================
-->
